    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0315" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/25812: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-18T12:00:00+01:00">November 18,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1823. My 1819, November 17, 8 p.m.,<anchor n="67" xml:id="d265-f1"/> and 1822,
                    November 18. It is perhaps superfluous for me to point out that the partial
                    mobilization decree with its preamble expressing Spain’s determination to defend
                    its integrity and sovereignty and to keep out of the war is a very favorable
                    development from our point of view.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
